WEBVTT

00:29.291 --> 00:30.958
It's not enough.

00:35.125 --> 00:36.666
It's not enough!

00:43.125 --> 00:45.208
Kokushu the Manslayer.

00:46.000 --> 00:47.958
I haven't had enough fun yet.

00:48.875 --> 00:50.916
Let's fight to the death.

00:53.208 --> 00:54.916
The war is already over.

00:58.208 --> 01:00.083
But we're samurai, aren't we?

01:00.875 --> 01:02.208
So we fight.

01:03.500 --> 01:06.666
It went by so fast.

01:07.375 --> 01:10.708
Those bastards
with their rifles and their cannons.

01:14.625 --> 01:15.625
See?

01:16.625 --> 01:18.875
That is all it takes.

01:18.958 --> 01:21.500
It doesn't even feel like killing.

01:21.583 --> 01:23.750
A neat and clean little weapon.

01:27.125 --> 01:29.500
The days of the sword
are coming to an end.

01:32.625 --> 01:35.041
The world doesn't need swordsmen like us.

01:35.541 --> 01:38.458
But that won't change who we truly are.

01:38.541 --> 01:41.166
You and I will always be manslayers,
no matter what.

01:43.750 --> 01:45.083
You killed this one, didn't you?

01:46.125 --> 01:47.375
Not bad at all.

01:48.958 --> 01:51.000
Why don't you show me how you do it?

02:24.666 --> 02:28.250
Is that enough to get you to fight?

02:54.458 --> 02:56.000
Go on, do it.

02:56.083 --> 02:57.416
Kill me.

03:02.791 --> 03:04.958
If you leave me here alive,

03:05.041 --> 03:07.958
I'll keep following you
to the ends of the earth.

03:12.041 --> 03:13.750
No. It's over.

03:24.625 --> 03:27.000
I will see you again!

03:28.291 --> 03:30.750
Saga Kokushu!

03:52.083 --> 03:54.041
The age of the samurai is over.

03:54.125 --> 03:56.125
You'll be locked in here until you die.

04:23.166 --> 04:25.916
I want to fight.

04:38.125 --> 04:39.625
Look how miserable you are,

04:40.458 --> 04:42.000
Kanjiya Bukotsu.

04:43.541 --> 04:45.916
You were gone for ten years,

04:46.000 --> 04:49.416
and then you decided to return
for the Satsuma Rebellion.

04:49.500 --> 04:51.750
You even killed your own allies.

04:55.000 --> 04:57.375
What has your life been like since then?

05:01.625 --> 05:05.041
You're asking me
what my life has been like?

05:07.541 --> 05:09.333
I've been dead

05:10.791 --> 05:12.708
for a while now.

05:15.583 --> 05:17.500
I bear good news.

05:17.583 --> 05:20.500
You'll have one more chance
to walk the path of the samurai.

05:23.166 --> 05:24.000
Huh?

05:34.708 --> 05:36.333
HOKOKU NEWSPAPER
PARTICIPANTS WANTED

06:01.375 --> 06:02.958
Hey! What's going on in here?

06:57.583 --> 06:58.750
TO TOSHIYOSHI KAWAJI

06:58.833 --> 07:02.375
WE MUST DISCUSS THE FUTURE OF THE POLICE.
I AWAIT YOU IN TOKYO.

07:05.958 --> 07:07.416
Lord Okubo!

07:12.333 --> 07:15.125
Lord Okubo, please listen to me.

07:15.208 --> 07:18.041
This rebellion is our chance
to finally destroy the samurai.

07:18.125 --> 07:21.250
We must exterminate them,
or else they will rebel once again.

07:21.333 --> 07:24.958
All I'm asking is for you
to grant us the right to carry guns.

07:26.416 --> 07:28.458
-I won't.
-Why not, sir?

07:29.000 --> 07:31.750
What will you do if one of them tries
to sneak in and assassinate you?

07:31.833 --> 07:33.125
How will we protect you?

07:33.208 --> 07:35.041
Have them forfeit their swords.

07:36.333 --> 07:38.541
-That is all I can allow.
-Okubo!

07:39.166 --> 07:42.375
We shouldn't use too heavy a hand.

07:42.458 --> 07:44.625
It will only lead to new uprisings.

07:44.708 --> 07:47.625
Remember Kyoto
during the shogunate's final days?

07:47.708 --> 07:50.416
Think of how many
of our comrades had fallen back then,

07:50.500 --> 07:53.000
killed by the swords of samurai assassins.

07:53.875 --> 07:55.250
Should they plot to kill us,

07:55.333 --> 07:57.291
we have no way
of defending ourselves against them.

07:57.375 --> 07:59.375
Their speed and power are unstoppable!

07:59.458 --> 08:03.666
We need to be able to bear firearms
for the sake of the future of Japan.

08:04.291 --> 08:07.458
There is no point
in fighting brute force with brute force!

08:08.333 --> 08:10.333
The future of Japan, you say.

08:10.416 --> 08:13.875
Do you know what Japan must have
in order to grow stronger as a nation?

08:13.958 --> 08:17.041
-The people, Kawaji!
-And the people need to be protected!

08:17.125 --> 08:19.333
You'll never win the people with violence!

08:19.416 --> 08:21.416
How can you not understand?

08:25.666 --> 08:26.666
Kawaji.

08:28.416 --> 08:30.541
The days of the samurai are done.

08:31.208 --> 08:32.291
However,

08:33.250 --> 08:36.833
if we cannot be united and live in peace,

08:40.083 --> 08:42.250
our nation will be destroyed.

09:05.083 --> 09:06.333
I will not give in.

09:07.291 --> 09:08.833
As long as I'm breathing.

09:58.791 --> 10:00.791
THE KODOKU PROJECT

10:10.541 --> 10:11.916
Lord Kawaji.

10:15.250 --> 10:16.250
Come in.

10:19.375 --> 10:20.958
Sorry to interrupt.

10:23.625 --> 10:26.208
Lord Okubo has sent you a telegram.

10:29.000 --> 10:31.166
To Kawaji Toshiyoshi.

10:31.250 --> 10:33.666
Need to discuss future of police.

10:33.750 --> 10:35.583
Awaiting you in Tokyo.

10:36.208 --> 10:37.750
Come promptly.

10:55.458 --> 10:57.958
There's something for everyone!
Miss, right this way!

11:24.625 --> 11:25.541
Futaba.

11:26.041 --> 11:26.958
Yes?

11:27.458 --> 11:28.458
You can go.

11:30.416 --> 11:31.416
Is that all right?

11:31.958 --> 11:32.958
Sure.

11:36.291 --> 11:37.750
Thank you so much.

11:41.916 --> 11:42.958
Are you sure?

11:44.000 --> 11:47.208
We have two days
before the appointment, and…

11:48.125 --> 11:50.250
these could be our last days together.

12:10.041 --> 12:12.666
Strange to see you
with that look on your face.

12:14.125 --> 12:15.333
What do you mean?

12:18.333 --> 12:21.583
You look like a father
who's worried about his child.

12:30.541 --> 12:33.166
Did having a family make you happy?

12:37.208 --> 12:38.208
Yes.

12:45.708 --> 12:48.000
What's it like having a real family?

13:20.000 --> 13:23.166
I was able to live life peacefully,
without killing anybody.

13:25.333 --> 13:28.500
So I would do
whatever it takes to save them.

13:38.333 --> 13:39.583
As for me…

13:42.583 --> 13:44.708
I've only been thinking of one thing.

13:47.166 --> 13:49.750
I should've just died
in the battle for succession.

13:50.250 --> 13:51.708
It'd be better than this life.

13:53.125 --> 13:54.166
Iroha.

13:54.791 --> 13:56.250
Don't say that. I didn't--

13:56.333 --> 13:57.416
Yes, I know.

14:01.208 --> 14:02.375
I know that.

14:07.458 --> 14:08.875
I'm going for a walk.

14:19.916 --> 14:21.791
What do you mean? What kind of trouble?

14:22.916 --> 14:24.416
Keep talking.

14:24.500 --> 14:26.541
Saga Shujiro and Kinugasa Iroha

14:27.125 --> 14:29.625
are going to die
unless you go and help them out.

14:31.750 --> 14:33.083
Wait, it's not…

14:33.708 --> 14:34.750
Gentosai, is it?

14:34.833 --> 14:37.625
Oh! Well done. That's the right answer.

14:37.708 --> 14:40.583
They're holding a festival
at the shrine just ahead.

14:40.666 --> 14:42.958
That's where the two of them are.

14:43.041 --> 14:45.000
Gentosai as well.

14:45.833 --> 14:46.916
Who are you?

14:47.791 --> 14:48.708
What do you want?

14:49.291 --> 14:50.541
Hmm…

14:51.333 --> 14:54.541
I'm not even sure anymore, honestly.

14:56.333 --> 14:57.708
You should hurry.

15:05.958 --> 15:07.083
Kyojin.

15:07.166 --> 15:10.208
Who are they?
What was all that? And who's Gentosai?

15:10.291 --> 15:11.166
Shinnosuke.

15:12.000 --> 15:15.333
In this world, some things are better
left kept in the dark, okay?

15:15.416 --> 15:16.291
But--

15:18.708 --> 15:21.000
Might as well just have some fun, right?

15:21.916 --> 15:24.083
After all, we're stuck in this Kodoku.

16:12.750 --> 16:16.875
The eighth successor of the Kyohachi-ryu,

16:16.958 --> 16:19.291
Kinugasa Iroha.

16:20.375 --> 16:22.000
I finally found you.

16:25.333 --> 16:26.708
Why is he here?

16:48.750 --> 16:50.708
All right, let's get started.

16:50.791 --> 16:52.000
Yes, sir!

16:53.000 --> 16:54.000
Here we go!

17:50.750 --> 17:52.833
We meet again at last.

17:55.833 --> 17:56.916
Kokushu!

18:03.708 --> 18:06.458
It's time
we settled this once and for all!

18:10.458 --> 18:13.125
Get back! Get back! Get back!

18:25.875 --> 18:27.333
Oh man.

18:28.208 --> 18:30.958
There's no thrill like trying
to kill each other, huh?

18:31.708 --> 18:33.916
You must be a beast
to find pleasure in murder.

18:34.000 --> 18:35.875
Yeah, but you're no different.

18:37.041 --> 18:39.250
And none of it matters.

18:39.333 --> 18:41.375
What's the point of anything anymore?

18:44.041 --> 18:47.250
I'll smash every bit
of this meaningless world!

18:47.333 --> 18:49.541
Stop this!

18:55.250 --> 18:57.125
What was that, darling?

18:58.458 --> 19:01.125
Why shed the blood
of those who have done nothing?

19:02.208 --> 19:03.458
That's not the samurai way!

19:03.541 --> 19:04.916
Futaba! Stand down!

19:06.916 --> 19:08.625
Then what is the samurai way?

19:14.125 --> 19:15.291
Come on, sweetheart.

19:15.375 --> 19:17.166
Tell me, what is it?

19:18.750 --> 19:20.916
Don't do it, Bukotsu. Let go of her.

19:22.541 --> 19:24.208
What if I killed her?

19:26.000 --> 19:27.833
I think that you'd fight me then, right?

19:27.916 --> 19:30.000
Don't. Stop this.

19:30.083 --> 19:31.541
Don't do it!

20:43.125 --> 20:44.291
Oh.

21:16.583 --> 21:18.333
Out of the way! Move!

21:35.541 --> 21:37.250
You can't win with your arm like that.

21:37.333 --> 21:38.833
Just give up.

21:40.875 --> 21:42.916
You're telling me to give up now?

21:44.708 --> 21:47.333
We ended up like this
all because we gave up, didn't we?

21:49.375 --> 21:51.916
How did you feel
when they took your sword away?

21:54.208 --> 21:56.333
Have you been happy with your life?

22:00.208 --> 22:02.833
-Yes, I truly have.
-Then why are you here?

22:04.666 --> 22:06.250
I'll tell you why.

22:06.750 --> 22:07.708
Because in the end,

22:07.791 --> 22:09.791
you're only worth something
if you can kill.

22:12.333 --> 22:15.125
You can't even save a single person
without killing.

22:21.208 --> 22:23.541
The age of the samurai is over?

22:24.416 --> 22:26.291
I say to hell with that.

22:26.791 --> 22:28.000
And even if it is,

22:29.291 --> 22:31.583
we will just rebuild it once again!

23:17.541 --> 23:18.541
Hmm.

23:47.458 --> 23:49.333
I found you.

24:20.875 --> 24:22.333
Out of the way!

24:28.541 --> 24:29.708
Run!

25:14.875 --> 25:16.708
That was an impressive strike.

25:19.708 --> 25:21.875
But this is the end for you.

25:22.375 --> 25:24.500
Do you have any last words?

25:27.291 --> 25:29.041
If that was your best,

25:31.125 --> 25:34.291
you'll never stand a chance
against my brothers.

25:35.458 --> 25:37.000
Oh really?

25:37.958 --> 25:41.500
Don't worry. Your siblings will be next.

26:11.250 --> 26:15.208
The fourth successor of the Kyohachi-ryu,

26:16.041 --> 26:18.125
Adashino Shikura.

26:36.875 --> 26:39.625
I can't believe he dodged that.

26:41.291 --> 26:43.541
The third successor,

26:45.500 --> 26:48.000
Gion Sansuke.

27:24.666 --> 27:26.708
Wretched monster!

27:42.333 --> 27:43.375
Sansuke.

27:44.833 --> 27:45.875
Move as one.

27:45.958 --> 27:47.000
Right.

28:00.041 --> 28:01.583
He's too strong.

28:04.000 --> 28:05.083
You run!

28:13.083 --> 28:15.208
Iroha! Let's move!

29:05.041 --> 29:06.500
Move!

31:40.541 --> 31:41.666
Move! Get back!

31:41.750 --> 31:43.833
Get back! Move!

31:43.916 --> 31:45.666
Get away! Come on!

31:49.250 --> 31:51.875
Move! It's not safe!

33:45.291 --> 33:48.250
Kokushu the Manslayer…

33:56.000 --> 33:57.500
At long last…

34:00.416 --> 34:03.000
I finally found happiness.

34:24.000 --> 34:25.958
Shujiro!

34:26.958 --> 34:29.708
Shujiro! Shujiro!

35:22.666 --> 35:24.916
The first participant to reach Chiryu was…

35:27.458 --> 35:30.083
227, Kamuykocha.

35:31.833 --> 35:34.250
Good! Yes, yes, very good!

35:34.333 --> 35:36.750
He didn't come all the way
from Ezo for nothing.

35:37.333 --> 35:40.916
We've received another report
that Kanjiya Bukotsu was just killed.

35:41.000 --> 35:43.750
-What? No!
-He was killed by 108, Saga Shujiro.

35:43.833 --> 35:46.833
-Oh!
-Well, such is the Manslayer we know.

35:46.916 --> 35:49.666
We've lost the Savage Slasher.
What a shame!

35:51.375 --> 35:54.583
Another ghost of the past has died,
nothing new.

35:56.666 --> 35:59.541
However, I'd say
that's still cause for celebration.

35:59.625 --> 36:01.666
I agree.

36:01.750 --> 36:03.291
Of course.

36:03.375 --> 36:06.333
Lord Kawaji, I think you should get going.

36:11.625 --> 36:13.500
Certain duties require my attention.

36:13.583 --> 36:16.583
So for now, I'll have
to leave you all to it, I'm afraid.

36:16.666 --> 36:19.208
Naturally. You're a busy man, of course.

36:19.291 --> 36:20.333
Sir,

36:21.208 --> 36:22.291
so it's finally time.

36:24.500 --> 36:28.458
I'm sure you'll be very entertained
as the Kodoku keeps unfolding.

36:49.583 --> 36:52.041
I've sent a telegram
informing them where to meet.

36:52.583 --> 36:53.583
Glad to hear it.

36:53.666 --> 36:55.750
Keep those wealthy fools
busy with their pleasures.

36:55.833 --> 36:57.208
As you command, sir.

37:11.916 --> 37:13.208
Come in.

37:14.666 --> 37:15.750
If I may.

37:18.333 --> 37:21.625
It seems Lord Kawaji is back.
He's just returned from his journey.

37:22.875 --> 37:25.458
I'll pay him a visit.
Get the carriage ready.

37:25.541 --> 37:26.625
Sir.

37:26.708 --> 37:28.958
Shinpei hasn't been in touch yet, has he?

37:30.083 --> 37:30.958
No, sir.

37:31.041 --> 37:33.625
We've checked at his home as well,
but he doesn't appear to be back.

37:33.708 --> 37:35.791
Should we have the police look for him?

37:38.125 --> 37:42.750
No. We'll search for him ourselves.
Inform the Home Ministry staff.

37:42.833 --> 37:43.666
Yes, sir.

38:36.291 --> 38:38.166
What are you--

38:49.875 --> 38:53.000
I know it's been awhile, Lord Okubo.

38:55.416 --> 38:57.625
Hanjiro, you're alive.

38:58.583 --> 38:59.833
I thought you were dead.

39:00.666 --> 39:04.750
Unfortunately,
Lord Kawaji will not be heading this way.

39:08.583 --> 39:09.625
What are you saying?

39:09.708 --> 39:14.166
He sent me instead.
And he asked me to deliver a message.

39:14.916 --> 39:16.125
"Farewell."

40:09.791 --> 40:10.916
What is this?

40:13.500 --> 40:15.416
What exactly is going on here?

40:18.083 --> 40:21.583
OKAZAKI-JUKU

40:24.750 --> 40:26.291
Shujiro.

40:26.375 --> 40:28.375
Do you think Iroha is doing okay?

40:28.875 --> 40:30.583
Knowing her,
I've no doubt she's all right.

40:32.208 --> 40:34.583
Extra! Extra!

40:34.666 --> 40:36.541
-Extra! Extra!
-What? What is it?

40:36.625 --> 40:37.583
Oh, give me one too.

40:37.666 --> 40:38.833
Extra!

40:38.916 --> 40:41.333
-One over here, please.
-Excuse me. Can I have one too?

40:41.416 --> 40:43.166
Extra! Extra!

40:43.666 --> 40:46.041
-This is most urgent news!
-Oh no. Wait.

40:46.125 --> 40:47.791
HOME MINISTER TOSHIMICHI OKUBO
ASSASSINATED

40:47.875 --> 40:49.500
Lord Okubo was killed?

40:51.541 --> 40:53.375
Who would do something like that?

40:56.541 --> 40:58.416
This is no coincidence.

40:59.458 --> 41:00.541
What?

41:02.000 --> 41:03.833
The Kodoku is related to this.

41:07.166 --> 41:08.541
Are you Mr. Saga?

41:10.500 --> 41:11.625
Yes, why?

41:11.708 --> 41:13.250
I have a message from Lord Maejima.

41:13.333 --> 41:16.625
"Returning to Tokyo. Urgent matter.
Make for the capital at once."

41:16.708 --> 41:18.000
That is all.

41:20.708 --> 41:21.958
I understand.

41:22.041 --> 41:23.666
If you'll excuse me.

41:27.541 --> 41:28.458
Futaba.

41:30.666 --> 41:33.083
We need to make it to Tokyo quickly.

41:35.333 --> 41:36.500
All right.

41:43.666 --> 41:45.750
Make way! Carriage coming through!

42:33.666 --> 42:35.083
Oh.

42:35.166 --> 42:37.500
Don't strain yourself.
The wound will reopen.

42:38.666 --> 42:39.750
Thank you.

42:51.208 --> 42:53.375
-Hey, you two.
-Hm?

42:56.166 --> 42:57.875
I had a dream last night.

43:00.500 --> 43:03.000
I saw us all living together as a family.

43:05.291 --> 43:08.458
Sansuke and I were arguing,
like we always did.

43:11.791 --> 43:13.541
Shikura was strong as always.

43:15.541 --> 43:17.875
We all used to smile a lot back then.

43:19.416 --> 43:21.625
Sure.

43:22.583 --> 43:23.958
We certainly did.

43:26.291 --> 43:28.875
Had we all fought each other
for the succession,

43:31.250 --> 43:33.041
I would not have survived.

43:39.458 --> 43:41.833
If Shujiro hadn't decided to run away…

43:47.083 --> 43:49.166
…I certainly wouldn't be alive right now.

43:56.125 --> 43:58.583
But unless we're able to defeat Gentosai,

44:01.250 --> 44:03.416
we will never manage to move forward.

44:16.541 --> 44:18.208
Once we're all together,

44:19.833 --> 44:21.583
we can finally take him down.

44:24.166 --> 44:25.375
You know it too.

44:27.958 --> 44:30.416
We cannot defeat him
unless we're together.

44:36.666 --> 44:38.166
You're right.

44:39.458 --> 44:40.708
And we'll do it.

44:41.666 --> 44:42.750
Yes.

44:43.416 --> 44:46.041
So now, we gather our brothers.

45:02.250 --> 45:04.958
-Oh!
-Attacked in Shimizudani.

45:05.041 --> 45:06.416
I can't believe he actually did it!

45:06.500 --> 45:08.916
Kawaji's a man of action, truly.
Wouldn't you agree?

45:09.000 --> 45:11.666
Now we can focus on the Kodoku in peace!

45:11.750 --> 45:12.875
Indeed.

45:13.458 --> 45:16.708
There are plenty
of remarkable contestants left to watch.

45:16.791 --> 45:18.708
The weak ones are gone.

45:18.791 --> 45:21.416
From here, only the strong remain.

45:28.791 --> 45:32.125
Well, well.

45:32.208 --> 45:34.458
CHIRYU, OKAZAKI, HAMAMATSU, SHIMADA

45:37.125 --> 45:38.333
Now, gentlemen.

45:38.833 --> 45:41.666
We guarantee this Kodoku
will keep you entertained.

45:43.000 --> 45:44.583
-Hear, hear.
-Hear, hear.

45:44.666 --> 45:46.916
-Hey! Wait for me!
-Go! Quick!

45:51.000 --> 45:53.708
Let's play some more.

45:57.166 --> 45:58.041
Well, lucky me.

45:59.041 --> 46:01.125
No one was around,
so I didn't get enough tags earlier.

46:09.916 --> 46:12.500
Good. That's enough for now.

46:14.375 --> 46:17.000
Oh. Do you want to fight, sir?

46:19.375 --> 46:20.375
It's fun!

46:20.458 --> 46:22.041
Come on. Why not?

46:49.250 --> 46:51.625
Well, well, so you couldn't get it done.

46:51.708 --> 46:53.958
Even with the tip I gave you, huh?

47:08.750 --> 47:12.250
Fight to the death,
until the last one standing.

47:37.750 --> 47:40.666
LAST SAMURAI STANDING

47:40.750 --> 47:43.416
THE END OF THE FIRST CHAPTER
